Subject: [PATCH] cpuidle: psci: keep CPU PM domains when set-suspend-mode fails

This board's secure firmware rejects PSCI_SET_SUSPEND_MODE (-95), and the
kernel treats that as fatal and rolls back the CPU/cluster power domains,
orphaning the SoC peripheral power-domain (st,stm32mp-pm-domain) and causing a
fatal deferred-probe storm (console/mmc/eth never probe). The domains register
fine and are all that's needed, so keep them when set-mode fails.

--- a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci-domain.c	2026-06-05 09:33:38.529186213 -0700
+++ b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci-domain.c	2026-06-05 09:33:38.513186105 -0700
@@ -174,8 +174,11 @@
 
 	/* let's try to enable OSI. */
 	ret = psci_set_osi_mode(use_osi);
-	if (ret)
-		goto remove_pd;
+	if (ret) {
+		pr_warn("psci: set %s mode failed (%d); keeping CPU PM domains\n",
+			use_osi ? "OSI" : "PC", ret);
+		ret = 0;
+	}
 
 	pr_info("Initialized CPU PM domain topology using %s mode\n",
 		use_osi ? "OSI" : "PC");
